        "# 14. Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "This analysis examined more than a decade of daily Gold and Silver price\n",
        "data using a quantitative time-series framework.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key areas of analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "- Historical return behavior\n",
        "- Rolling annualized volatility\n",
        "- Historical drawdowns\n",
        "- Long-term 200-day price trends\n",
        "- ±2σ trend-based price bands\n",
        "- Deviation from long-term trend\n",
        "- Volatility regimes\n",
        "- Gold–Silver return correlation\n",
        "- Gold/Silver price ratio\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key observations\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis provides a quantitative framework for comparing the risk and\n",
        "price behavior of Gold and Silver across different market conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "In particular, rolling volatility and drawdown analysis highlight periods\n",
        "of elevated market risk, while the 200-day moving average and price bands\n",
        "provide a statistical reference for identifying large deviations from\n",
        "long-term price trends.\n",
        "\n",
        "The results should be interpreted as historical and descriptive analysis.\n",
        "They do not constitute investment advice or a prediction of future prices.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Yahoo Finance futures data may differ from local physical or MCX prices.\n",
        "2. USD-to-INR conversion introduces currency effects into INR-denominated\n",
        "   prices.\n",
        "3. Rolling volatility and price bands are backward-looking measures.\n",
        "4. The ±2σ bands are descriptive and do not imply a trading signal.\n",
        "5. Transaction costs, taxes, liquidity, storage costs, and other real-world\n",
        "   investment frictions are not modeled.\n",
        "6. Correlation and historical volatility can change substantially across\n",
        "   market regimes."
      ]
